{"nodes": [{"id": "supabase_functions_fn_create_transport_run_fn_create_transport_run", "label": "fn_create_transport_run", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_create_transport_run.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Card ^ref-22 / M2, BR16, D04.1: creates the vehicle, its fare and the method that will split that fare \u2014 and no lines. The p_lot_ids array is taken, checked and discarded so R26 can be asked ONCE over the whole array at run creation rather than per line after three lines already exist (TC-10): a CM_TO_FOODIVA run is refused unless every lot on it is RETURN_SCHEDULED, which is what BR17 means by the return leg existing only once someone entitled to do so has named a receive date. alloc_method is SNAPSHOTTED here from dated config and is not a parameter (R29, BR23): a caller who can choose the method can choose differently for two runs on the same day, and more importantly fn_allocate_freight reads the method off this row so a later config change cannot move a closed number. CONFIG_NOT_SET propagates rather than defaulting (ADR-023). R25's branch-leg-carries-no-fare is raised by name as well as enforced by transport_runs_branch_leg_free, so an Owner reads a rule rather than a constraint name. R4 idempotency mirrors fn_add_po_delivery, including the unique_violation fallback where the losing session reads the winner's row."}], "edges": [{"source": "supabase_functions_fn_create_transport_run_fn_create_transport_run", "target": "supabase_functions_fn_require_owner_fn_require_owner", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_create_transport_run.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_functions_fn_create_transport_run_fn_create_transport_run", "target": "supabase_functions_fn_config_value_fn_config_value", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED